    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1536">

                <pb facs="0987" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/44.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the French Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt, in due course, of the Ambassador’s note of the 20th ultimo, with which
                    was enclosed a copy of a communication addressed to him by two French priests
                    and a Spanish priest, giving an account of the treatment accorded to them by the
                    Mexican authorities at Saltillo and furnishing much information as to general
                    conditions in Mexico.</p>
                <p>The Department is extremely grateful to the Ambassador for having furnished it
                    with this information.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
